<DocLayout slug={slug} title={title} description={description}>

[nvh-tailwindcss](https://github.com/ezTxmMC/nvh-tailwindcss) brings Tailwind CSS 4.3 to nvh projects. It is a Novus dependency: no Node, no `node_modules`. It runs the official standalone Tailwind binary (pinned to 4.3.3, downloaded once into `~/.novus/tools/tailwindcss/4.3.3/` and checked against its sha256) and adds what the bare CLI lacks for nvh sources.

## Wiring

```nv
require "github.com/ezTxmMC/nvh-tailwindcss" "latest"
replace "github.com/ezTxmMC/nvh-tailwindcss" "../nvh-tailwindcss"   // a local checkout, optional
```

```nv
import "github.com/ezTxmMC/nvh-tailwindcss/tailwindcss"

method buildStyles() {
    var options = tailwindcss.options("styles/site.css", "public/site.css")
    options..minify = true
        ..sources = ["../nvh-markdown"]
    var result = tailwindcss.build(options)
    if (result.ok == false) {
        eprintln result.output
    }
}
```

The layout links the result with `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/site.css">` (or `tailwindcss.link(href)`). `tailwindcss.watch(options)` rebuilds in the background while the dev server runs.

## Why not just the CLI?

Tailwind finds classes by scanning text, and nvh writes some of them in ways it does not understand:

| nvh source | handed to Tailwind |
|---|---|
| `class:bg-primary-500={active}` | `bg-primary-500` |
| `class="px-4 {extra} hover:underline"` | `px-4`, `hover:underline` |
| `"flex items-center gap-2"` in `.nv` or `.nvh` | its classes, when the whole string is a class list |

The package scans `.nvh`, `.nvmd` and `.nv` files and every extra source, writes `.nvh-tailwind/candidates.html` and an input CSS that registers it with `@source`. Add `.nvh-tailwind/` to your `.gitignore`.

## A theme

Tailwind 4 is configured in CSS. This site defines its three purples as tokens:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
    --color-primary-500: oklch(0.62 0.24 295);
    --color-secondary-500: oklch(0.60 0.23 265);
    --color-accent-500: oklch(0.66 0.25 330);
}
```

and uses them as `bg-primary-500`, `text-accent-300`, `border-secondary-400` anywhere in a component.

## Command line

```sh
novusc run tailwind.nv install
novusc run tailwind.nv build --input styles/site.css --output public/site.css --minify
novusc run tailwind.nv watch --input styles/site.css --output public/site.css
```

<Callout type="tip" title="Standalone plugins">
The standalone binary bundles `@tailwindcss/typography` and `@tailwindcss/forms`: `@plugin "@tailwindcss/typography";`.
</Callout>


</DocLayout>
